 "text": "Without speculation, generating several tokens requires several sequential decoding steps. With speculation, one verification pass can accept multiple tokens. We haven't necessarily reduced the total computation, in fact, drafting and verification introduce extra work. But we've reduced the number of expensive sequential steps. And on GPUs, verifying multiple tokens together can make better use of parallel computation.",
